    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who headlines the lineup with a 74.56 efficiency score against a favorable 5.25 xERA matchup against Bieber. **Drake Baldwin** also earns elite status (68.29) thanks to his elevated leadoff position and a juicy matchup against Pfaadt. While the squad faces a few tactical hurdles, the optimizer remains aggressive on hitters like **Kyle Tucker** (66.11) and **Andy Pages** (65.77), both of whom benefit from wind-aided conditions that bolster their base projections despite facing a moderate threat in Gasser. **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Robert Jr.** provide critical depth, with the latter\u2019s 63.27 score benefiting significantly from a platoon advantage against Alvarez, effectively balancing his exposure to an elite-hold pitcher.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Jackson Merrill**, who finished with a 50.88 score. While **Jackson Merrill** holds strong utility value, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected floor of **Jacob Wilson** (64.06) and **Coby Mayo** (60.18). **Jacob Wilson** specifically capitalized on a strong park factor and a top-three lineup slot that makes him a more efficient play than the bottom-half positioning of our bench pieces. We are proceeding with caution regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations; **Kyle Tucker**, **Wade Meckler**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson** all carry variance risks depending on final manager decisions. Additionally, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.98) has a challenging matchup against Cole, his BvP history keeps his floor stable, though he is the most susceptible to a total collapse if the high-tier pitching suppresses our scoring across the board.",
